# Environment Variables Setup

## Local Development (.env.local)

Create a `.env.local` file in the root directory:

```
# Database
DATABASE_URL=mysql://root:password@localhost:3306/kklogistics_dev

# Server
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000

# Optional: OAuth (if integrating)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-github-client-id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your-github-client-secret

# Optional: AWS S3 (for file uploads)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-aws-key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-aws-secret
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
S3_BUCKET_NAME=your-bucket-name

# Optional: Manus Analytics
VITE_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT=https://analytics.example.com
VITE_ANALYTICS_WEBSITE_ID=your-website-id
```

## Production - Railway.app

Set these in Railway dashboard under "Variables":

```
DATABASE_URL=mysql://user:pass@gateway.railway.app:3306/railway
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=8080
```

## Production - DigitalOcean

Set these in App Platform dashboard:

```
DATABASE_URL=mysql://dbuser:dbpassword@db-mysql-xxxxxxx.a.db.ondigitalocean.com:25060/defaultdb
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
```

## Production - AWS

Create Systems Manager Parameter Store entries or use .env file:

```
DATABASE_URL=mysql://admin:password@mydb.xxxxx.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com:3306/kklogistics
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
```

## Notes

- ⚠️ Never commit `.env.local` to Git
- ⚠️ Keep secrets in environment variables, not code
- ✅ Use `.env.example` to show required variables
- ✅ Each hosting platform provides connection strings

## Getting DATABASE_URL for Each Platform

### Railway.app
1. Go to your project dashboard
2. Click on "MySQL" service
3. Click "Connect"
4. Copy the connection string

### DigitalOcean
1. Go to Databases
2. Click your MySQL database
3. Click "Connection Details"
4. Copy the connection string

### AWS RDS
1. Go to RDS Dashboard
2. Click your database instance
3. Look for "Endpoint" 
4. Format: `mysql://admin:password@endpoint:3306/dbname`

### Local MySQL
```
mysql://root:password@localhost:3306/kklogistics_dev
```

Or with Docker:
```
mysql://root:password@host.docker.internal:3306/kklogistics_dev
```
